Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt76x02: preserve a published group WCID on re-add

The MMIO restart path removes station WCIDs but leaves the
interface group WCIDs published. The TX worker resumes before
mac80211 adds the interfaces back, so a group WCID can still own
pending packets or be linked into the TX status list at that
point.

Reinitializing the interface private data overwrites those live
list links, packet IDs and queue state. Preserve a group WCID if
the interface's slot still points to that same object. Normal
remove/add still initializes it, since remove_interface
unpublishes and cleans up the old WCID.

Keeping the live object avoids a teardown racing with workers or
RCU readers. Reconfiguration restores the hardware state and keys
separately.

Assisted-by: LLM

---
diff --git a/mt76x02_util.c b/mt76x02_util.c
--- a/mt76x02_util.c
+++ b/mt76x02_util.c
@@ -294,6 +294,13 @@
 {
 	struct mt76x02_vif *mvif = (struct mt76x02_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct mt76_txq *mtxq;
+
+	/* The restart path leaves the group WCID published. Keep its queues
+	 * and list links intact while mac80211 adds the interface back.
+	 */
+	if (rcu_access_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[MT_VIF_WCID(idx)]) ==
+	    &mvif->group_wcid)
+		return;
 
 	memset(mvif, 0, sizeof(*mvif));
 
